---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { parse as parseYaml } from 'yaml';
import AboutTabs from '../../components/AboutTabs.astro';
import Shell from '../../components/Shell.astro';
import { aboutCounts, countedNoun, countWord, joinAnd, numberBadge, shortSourceName } from '../../lib/about-stats.mjs';
import { formatRunStamp, latestWeek, synthesisExcerpt } from '../../lib/weeks';

const week = latestWeek();
if (!week) {
  throw new Error('About needs a published week');
}

const sourceFile = parseYaml(readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), 'config', 'sources.yaml'), 'utf8'));
const enabled = (sourceFile?.sources ?? []).filter((source) => source && source.enabled === true);
const aiOnly = enabled.filter((source) => source.ai_only === true);
const aiOnlyNames = aiOnly.map((source) => shortSourceName(source.display_name));
const counts = aboutCounts(week);
const sourcesTotal = enabled.length;
const badge = numberBadge(counts);
const runSum = `${counts.stories} + ${counts.merged} + ${counts.alsoSeen} + ${counts.leftOut} = ${counts.considered}`;
const consideredLabel = `${countedNoun(counts.considered, 'item', 'items')} considered`;
const storiesLabel = `${countedNoun(counts.stories, 'story', 'stories')} (${counts.merged} more merged in as also covered)`;
const alsoSeenLabel = `${counts.alsoSeen} Also seen ${counts.alsoSeen === 1 ? 'link' : 'links'}`;
const themesLabel = countedNoun(counts.themes, 'theme', 'themes');
const picksLabel = countedNoun(counts.picks, 'pick', 'picks');
const storiesCountLabel = countedNoun(counts.stories, 'story', 'stories');
const aiOnlySentence = `${countWord(aiOnly.length)} ${
  aiOnly.length === 1 ? 'source is' : 'sources are'
} set so items not about AI stay out: ${joinAnd(aiOnlyNames)}.`;
const ranAt = formatRunStamp(week.generated_at);
---

<Shell
  title="About: how it works · Dan's AI Digest"
  description={synthesisExcerpt(week.briefing.synthesis)}
  canonical="/about/how-it-works"
  week={week}
  active="about"
  scope="latest"
>
  <AboutTabs tab="how-it-works" />
  <div class="g hph">
    <p
      class="run"
      data-considered={counts.considered}
      data-stories={counts.stories}
      data-merged={counts.merged}
      data-also-seen={counts.alsoSeen}
      data-left-out={counts.leftOut}
      data-themes={counts.themes}
      data-picks={counts.picks}
      data-sources={sourcesTotal}
      data-ai-only={aiOnly.length}
    >
      <span class="ri">{consideredLabel}</span>
      <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <span class="ri">{storiesLabel}</span>
      <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <span class="ri">{alsoSeenLabel}</span>
      <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <span class="ri">{counts.leftOut} left out</span>
      <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <span class="ri">{themesLabel}</span>
    </p>
    <p class="runnote">
      {runSum}. Some items are filtered out before review and aren't in this count: anything outside the Sunday to
      Saturday week, source-level filters (for example Latent Space AINews and subscriber-only posts), and items not
      about AI from the {aiOnly.length} sources set to AI only. A passing mention from any other source is a rubric
      call and counts in the {counts.leftOut}.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="g hbody">
    <section class="steps-col" aria-labelledby="steps-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="steps-h">Each week, in order</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step" id="sources">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Dan picks the sources</h3>
            <p>
              Dan chooses every feed the digest reads, <a href="/about/sources" data-source-total={sourcesTotal}
                >{sourcesTotal} right now</a
              > across newsletters, blogs and YouTube channels. Nothing outside that list gets in, and changing it takes
              Dan's approval. A validator test pins the {sourcesTotal} approved sources.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="filters">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Source filters<span class="cnt">before counting</span></h3>
            <p>
              Items outside the Sunday to Saturday week are dropped. Some sources have their own filters, such as Latent
              Space's AINews and subscriber-only posts. {aiOnlySentence} These items are never counted. A passing-mention
              item from any other source is a rubric call and counts in the {counts.leftOut} left out.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="rules">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Inclusion rubric<span class="cnt">{counts.leftOut} left out</span></h3>
            <p>
              The AI checks each counted item: it has to be new, argued, or relevant to a running story. Each one gets a
              yes or no plus a one-line reason. Version bumps and quote-only posts never reach Also seen.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="merge">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Grouping<span class="cnt">{counts.merged} merged in, {counts.alsoSeen} to Also seen</span></h3>
            <p>
              Writeups of the same story become one, and one URL belongs to one item. Thin items (video descriptions or
              feed items with no article body) are marked during grouping. {counts.alsoSeen} went to Also seen. The lead
              source is picked in order: a full card beats a thin link, a piece about the story beats a roundup, then the
              source stating the key facts wins. Excluded items are never added back.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="summaries">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Each story is summarized<span class="cnt">{storiesCountLabel}</span></h3>
            <p>
              A summary of 60 words or fewer and a one-sentence takeaway, from that source only. On a merged story the
              takeaway uses the main item's summary.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="themes">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Lead and themes<span class="cnt">{themesLabel}</span></h3>
            <p>
              The lead and the five themes are written together: one to three sentences, then five rows of a short label
              and one 25 to 35 word sentence. Which themes is the AI's judgment, and a story can sit in two.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="top5">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">7</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Top 5<span class="cnt">{picksLabel}</span></h3>
            <p>The AI picks five full stories. It is the AI's judgment, with no scoring formula and no defined rank order.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="number">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">8</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Number of the week<span class="cnt" data-number={badge}>{badge}</span></h3>
            <p>
              Figures from the week are scored on five tests: it changes the picture, it is firsthand, it has a
              comparison, it is about something real, and it will still matter in a month. Required from W42 on.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="snote">Steps 6 to 8 are not done in a fixed order.</li>
        <li class="step" id="check">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">9</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Schema check</h3>
            <p>The week file is built and validated. The checks pass: the week schema and the static site build.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="publish">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">10</span>
          <div>
            <h3>The week file is merged</h3>
            <p>A PR that changes only that file is opened, and it merges automatically once the checks pass, with no person reviewing it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step" id="deploy">
          <span class="sn" aria-hidden="true">11</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Vercel deploys</h3>
            <p>The site rebuilds from the merged week file and goes live.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <aside class="side-col">
      <section aria-labelledby="rules-h">
        <h2 class="h2" id="rules-h">Inclusion rules</h2>
        <p class="sub">An item gets in if it meets at least one:</p>
        <ul class="rl">
          <li><b>New.</b> A launch, a finding, a policy move, or real data.</li>
          <li><b>Argued.</b> A real argument or analysis, not just a pointer to someone else's.</li>
          <li><b>Relevant.</b> It touches a theme from this week or a running story.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="sub">Left out:</p>
        <ul class="rl">
          <li>Shorts with no substance.</li>
          <li>Quotes with no commentary.</li>
          <li>Minor version releases.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="sub">
          Version bumps and quote-only posts do not appear in Also seen either, and grouping never brings back an excluded
          item.
        </p>
        <p class="sub">There is no cap on how many items one source can contribute.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="wrong-h" class="wrong">
        <h2 class="h2" id="wrong-h">What it can get wrong</h2>
        <ul class="rl">
          <li>
            It can misjudge what counts as new or argued and leave out a good piece. Every exclusion keeps its reason, so
            it can be checked.
          </li>
          <li>Merging can join two different stories, or miss that two writeups are the same one.</li>
          <li>Short summaries drop nuance. Check the source before quoting a figure.</li>
          <li>
            A weekly PR that only adds that week's file merges automatically once the checks pass, with no person reviewing
            it.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <p class="hfoot">Runs Sundays at 7:29 AM ET. This week ran {ranAt}.</p>
</Shell>
